Job Description:
Location:
Kaduna North
Details
Centre for Community Development and Research Network (CCDRN), a National Non-Governmental Organization (NNGO) seeks a Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Learning (MEAL) Officer to Support its Organization M&E Unit.
The MEAL Officer will support the development, implementation, and refinement of CCDRN MEAL system and manage performance monitoring, adaptive management, and evaluations.
S/he will support the coordination of field monitoring and expert assessments, capacity strengthening, and other personnel responsible for monitoring performance, and the development and implementation of data management systems.
Reporting & Supervision:
The Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Learning Officer will report to the M&E Manager.
Primary Responsibilities
Support design, implementation, and strengthening of CCDRN MEAL systems
Support development of program indicators and targets;
Work closely with the M&E Manager to conduct research and program evaluation across CCDRN targeted communities’ in-line with donors/partners requirement.
Monitor and analyze program implementation progress, and timely data collection;
Develop and implement a learning agenda across all the technical components of the CCDRN projects in-line with donors requirement;
Support capacity building of program and M&E team to carry out activities;
Contribute to program efforts to build the technical, systems, and operational capacity relevant stakeholders on the development and implementation of program data management systems;
Conduct field visits, as necessary, to develop monitoring/performance management plans with technical teams;
Produce regular communication of MEAL activities to program team and partners
Perform other related duties as assigned.
Required Skills & Qualifications
Bachelor's Degree required. An advanced degree in education or social sciences is preferred;
Proven skills in qualitative and quantitative analysis, as well as capacity building experience;
Significant experience in data collection, dissemination methodologies, and the creation of indicator targets;
Previous NGO experience and a strong knowledge of donors reporting requirements is an advantage; and
Excellent interpersonal skills and teamwork. Effective communication skills, able to make formal and informal presentations both orally and in writing and produce professional and analytical reports and program documents.
Willingness to travel to any part of the country especially northeast Nigeria
Minimum of 3-10 years work experience.
